<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <!-- D1 (narrowed): EI_EXPOSE_REP and EI_EXPOSE_REP2 off everywhere except ram.document.template.
         The rule objects to a class handing out, or keeping, a reference to a mutable object someone else holds.
         Outside the template package, every such reference in Project Pulse is shared on purpose:
         - JPA entities (144 of the 219): Hibernate tracks changes through the very collection and association
           objects the entity holds, and the services edit entities through those getters
           (section.getInstructors(), course.addInstructor(...)). A defensive copy would make those edits vanish.
         - Spring beans (29): a constructor-injected bean is a singleton meant to be shared.
         - DTO records and report carriers (44, e.g. UseCaseDto, PeerEvaluationAverage, MyUserPrincipal): built
           by a converter or service inside one request, serialized, and dropped; nothing keeps them afterwards.
         The template package is different: DocumentTemplateRegistry loads each template from YAML once and hands the
         same DocumentTemplate to every request. That is the shared mutable state the rule exists for, so it stays
         enforced there. -->
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
        <Not><Package name="team.projectpulse.ram.document.template"/></Not>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
